  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0598ed51-73a4-44ac-8f7e-6cd5128542d5"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the vertices of the subgraph ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " that have an edge in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " which is not an edge of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"5a04ab80-8238-41d5-9716-935f250d0376"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the inner vertex boundary of a set ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " of vertices of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " is \[PartialD]",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " = {",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " : some neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " lies outside ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 "}. It lies in ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " \[Backslash] \[PartialD]",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["GraphInterior"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/GraphInterior", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "82240130-9786-47ae-ab7c-9a681057e905"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"33e7dccc-c0ef-48a4-b92f-cbe28a7299f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A subgraph ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " is read with its own edges: a vertex of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 " is a boundary vertex when some edge of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " at it is not an edge of ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 ". For an induced subgraph the two readings agree; a sparser subgraph has \
more boundary, and in a tiling every vertex of a path is a boundary vertex."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ece7aa5c-5648-4c94-a8cf-5da5bca1b59d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The outer boundary of ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 ", the vertices outside ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " next to it, is the boundary of the complement. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraBoundary"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBoundary", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ef1e9252-d521-4b93-93c6-999126469c43"],
 " with its default method is the boundary of the vertex set, sorted; it \
reads a subgraph by its vertices. The boundary is one-sided, unlike the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["TopologicalBoundary"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/TopologicalBoundary", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "63638b5a-cb04-44f8-b3e7-22c6bcf0b92e"],
 " of the ball topology, which lies on both sides of a set."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"14bc89ad-f738-4f7a-b027-d8541bdc3cd6"]
}, Open  ]],

